WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.603
After a spacewalk, the danger isn't over.

2
00:00:03.643 --> 00:00:05.256
Here's what to watch for.

3
00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:11.032
To stay flexible, the spacesuit runs at a
much lower pressure than the cabin.

4
00:00:11.072 --> 00:00:12.483
About a third of it.

5
00:00:13.383 --> 00:00:15.389
Like a diver coming up too fast,

6
00:00:15.389 --> 00:00:18.773
the nitrogen dissolved in your blood can
form bubbles.

7
00:00:19.673 --> 00:00:21.512
That's decompression sickness.

8
00:00:21.552 --> 00:00:24.974
To prevent it, you breathe pure oxygen
before going

9
00:00:24.974 --> 00:00:27.255
out: it flushes the nitrogen away.

10
00:00:27.295 --> 00:00:29.835
This preparation can take a few hours.

11
00:00:30.735 --> 00:00:33.690
Even so, watch your body in the hours
after.

12
00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:40.017
Joint pain, itchy skin, tingling, or
unusual tiredness are warning signs.

13
00:00:40.057 --> 00:00:42.172
They can appear several hours later.

14
00:00:43.072 --> 00:00:45.387
Any of these? Tell Keiko right away.

15
00:00:45.427 --> 00:00:47.855
Treatment works best when it starts early.

16
00:00:48.755 --> 00:00:50.767
Don't tough it out: report it.

